  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "A car salesman has sold the following quantities of a particular model of car in the last few weeks:\n\n$$\n3,\\,5,\\,6,\\,8,\\,5,\\,3\n$$\n\nWhat is the mean of these figures?",
  "worked_solution": "If we have a data set that consists of the points ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},\u2026,{x}_{n},$ then the mean is denoted by $\\overset{\u2015}{x}$ and is given by the following formula:\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{x}=\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i}\n$$\n\nHere, there are $n=6$ data points. Adding up all the points in the data set, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{6}{x}_{i} & =3+5+6+8+5+3 \\\\  & =30.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the mean is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\u2015}{x} & =\\frac{1}{n}{\\sum }_{i=1}^{n}{x}_{i} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}\\cdot 30 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
